            <div xml:id="d619">

                <pb facs="0975" n="1933" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1933"/>

                <head>No. 57.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 19, 1887</date>.
                        (Received November 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 625.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your circular instruction of
                    July 9 with reference to the amendment of the laws relating to shipping, I have
                    the honor to acquaint you that I lost no time in forwarding a copy of the same
                    to Her Majesty’s Government and in inviting their cooperation in the matter. The
                    Marquis of Salisbury’s reply to my communication has just reached me, and I
                    inclose herewith a copy of the same.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d619-a1.xml" xpointer="d619-a1"/>
            </div>
